ENGLISH (translation; the Czech original below governs)
──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

The mailmcp software (the "Software"), including its source code, is the
Author's copyrighted work. It is distributed as a prebuilt package; on
request the Author makes the source code available to customers for
inspection, review and modification for their own installation. THIS IS NOT
OPEN SOURCE. By installing or using the Software you accept this agreement.

1. Grant of license
   Upon payment of the license fee the Author grants you a non-exclusive,
   non-transferable license to install and run the Software within the tier
   purchased:
   0) Free (no licence key): you may install and run the Software without
      payment, with at most 5 mailboxes per configuration or user token; every
      message the Software composes carries the "Sent with mailmcp.ai"
      signature, which you may not remove or alter. Sections 3, 4 (except
      4a), 7, 8 and 9 apply to Free use as well.
   a) Personal: one running installation (one server or one device) for one
      natural person, at most 5 mailboxes in the configuration or in each
      user token.
   b) Unlimited: one running installation in shared-server mode for an
      unlimited number of users and mailboxes within one organization, team
      or course; commercial use inside the organization is permitted.
   Each additional running installation requires an additional license. A
   license may be moved to another installation at any time as long as you
   never have more running installations than licenses.

2. License key
   The Software requires a license key issued by the Author. The key is
   verified locally; the Software does not contact the Author. The key is
   confidential; do not publish or share it beyond the installation it was
   issued for.

3. What you may do
   You may modify the Software for your own installation and you may read
   and audit the source code.

4. What you may not do
   You may not a) run the Software without a valid key or beyond the tier
   purchased, b) remove, bypass or disable the license verification,
   c) distribute, sell, rent, sublicense or publish the Software or works
   derived from it, d) offer the Software to third parties as a service
   (hosting, SaaS) outside your own organization without a separate
   agreement with the Author, e) remove copyright notices.

5. Updates
   Updates are included up to the next major version (e.g. 0.x → 1.0). A
   major upgrade may carry a fee; you may keep using older releases.

6. Refunds
   Within 60 days of purchase the Author refunds the full price on request;
   the license then ends and you must stop using the Software.

7. Warranty and liability
   The Software is provided "as is", without warranty. The Author is not
   liable for lost profit, lost data or indirect damages; the Author's total
   liability is limited to the fees you paid for the license in the most
   recent twelve months. The Software operates on your mail accounts; you
   are responsible for passwords, permissions and the content of messages
   sent.

8. Termination
   The license ends upon breach; you must uninstall and stop using the
   Software. Sections 4, 7 and 9 survive termination.

9. Governing law
   This agreement is governed by the laws of the Czech Republic; disputes go
   to the courts competent for the Author's seat. Consumers keep the rights
   granted by Czech and EU law, which this agreement does not limit.

